    "id": "news-1788441091253-7",
    "title": "SalamAir Launches Direct Flights Connecting Mogadishu and Muscat",
    "original_title": "Duulimaadyo Toos ah oo Maanta Ka Billowday Muqdisho iyo Muscat",
    "slug": "salamair-launches-direct-flights-connecting-mogadishu-and-muscat",
    "summary": "Omani carrier SalamAir has started direct flights between Mogadishu and Muscat, a first for Somalia-Oman aviation links. The service operates twice weekly, with one-way tickets starting at 79.99 Omani riyals.",
    "content": "On Thursday, September 3, 2026, the Omani airline SalamAir officially inaugurated direct flights between Mogadishu and Muscat, the capitals of Somalia and Oman. This new route marks the first time an uninterrupted air link has connected the two countries, with services scheduled twice a week. The airline has set introductory one-way fares at 79.99 Omani riyals, roughly equivalent to $208.\n\nSalamAir, a low-cost carrier based in Muscat, has been expanding its network across the region. The launch follows months of discussions between Somali and Omani aviation authorities, part of broader efforts to boost bilateral trade and movement. The route is expected to cater not only to direct travelers but also to those using Muscat as a gateway to onward destinations in the Gulf and beyond.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development is significant. Many Somalis reside in Gulf states, and direct flights reduce travel time and the hassle of connecting through hubs like Dubai or Doha. The affordable pricing also makes visits to family in Somalia more accessible for those living in Oman. Additionally, the route could stimulate business exchanges and investment, as Muscat becomes a more convenient entry point to the Somali market.\n\nThe introduction of these flights is part of a wider trend of improved aviation connectivity in the Horn of Africa, which has seen new carriers and routes emerge in recent years. It also reflects Oman's growing engagement with Africa, as the sultanate seeks to strengthen economic and cultural ties. For diaspora members, this new link represents a tangible step toward closer ties between their countries of residence and origin.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/03/duulimaadyo-toos-ah-oo-maanta-ka-billowday-muqdisho-iyo-muscat/",
